      "unordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Dual Process Theory:** The foundational concept of \"System 1\" (fast, intuitive) and \"System 2\" (slow, deliberate) thinking, which is central to understanding *why* biases exist and *how* they function.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 103,
          "source": "topic-set_metacognition-cognitive-biases-and-logical-fallacies_🆔20251105182355.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Heuristics:** A deeper dive into the specific mental shortcuts themselves (e.g., Availability Heuristic, Representativeness Heuristic) that form the basis of many cognitive biases.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 107,
          "source": "topic-set_metacognition-cognitive-biases-and-logical-fallacies_🆔20251105182355.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Cognitive Dissonance:** The psychological discomfort experienced when holding two conflicting beliefs, a state which logical fallacies are often unconsciously employed to \"resolve.\"",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 114,
          "source": "topic-set_metacognition-cognitive-biases-and-logical-fallacies_🆔20251105182355.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Epistemic Humility:** The practice of recognizing the limits of one's own knowledge and the high probability of being wrong. This is often considered a prerequisite state for effective metacognition.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 116,
          "source": "topic-set_metacognition-cognitive-biases-and-logical-fallacies_🆔20251105182355.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Bayesian Updating:** A formal, probabilistic model for how to *correctly* update one's beliefs in the face of new evidence, serving as a mathematical antidote to biases like Confirmation Bias.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 116,
          "source": "topic-set_metacognition-cognitive-biases-and-logical-fallacies_🆔20251105182355.md"
        }
      ]
    },
